  "summary": "Fox-IT and NCC Group describe a financially motivated Lazarus subgroup that uses social engineering against cryptocurrency and DeFi organisations and deploys three RATs: PondRAT, ThemeForestRAT and RemotePE. Persistence is achieved through phantom DLL loading of a custom PerfhLoader via the SessionEnv (or IKEEXT) service, and the actor layers custom and public tooling such as keyloggers, a Chromium credential dumper, Proxymini, frpc and Mimikatz. PondRAT is a simple HTTP(S) RAT with XOR+Base64 messaging, ThemeForestRAT is a stealthier in-memory second stage with an RC4-encrypted configuration file, and RemotePE is a DPAPI-keyed, later-stage RAT on three platforms.",
